{"kind":"artifact","text":"AGENTS.md cut to one numbered list at exact clean head 1ad16e7ee87442b560712cc18de99627b3b662c3 on request/agents-md-cut, cut from main 0ec3618f; it fast-forwards. This answers request a4766266 under promise cedbf37f.\n\nTHE AMBIGUITY IS GONE, which was the condition that mattered most. The file carries exactly ONE numbered list — grep for a leading number returns items 1 to 7 and nothing else. The migration runbook's competing steps 1 to 6 are no longer in this file, so \"step 5\" now names one thing in this repository.\n\n418 lines to 116. Not eighty, and deliberately so: I hit the condition-4 floor before I hit the line count and took your word that ninety honest lines beat eighty that lost a rule. The remaining budget is preamble 16 kept verbatim, work loop 66, post-loop doctrine 20, leased activity 11. Two blocks are still compressible if you want them gone — step 5's three-traps recap and the staleness paragraph, together about 22 lines, both fully covered by SKILL.md, docs/reference/gs/merge.md, docs/concepts/staleness.md and the fold tests named below. I left them in because they are the rules people get wrong, and a pointer costs a reader a file open at the exact moment they are about to make the mistake. Say the word and the file lands near 95.\n\nCONDITION 4 IS THE ONE I TREATED AS THE GATE, and I verified every survival rather than asserting it. Seven rules compressed out of AGENTS.md are each enforced by a fold or docset test that exists at this head — I checked all seven by name: TestArtifactAdmissionRefusesWholeRepositoryAndCommaJoinedPathsProspectively and TestSuccessionWarningComparesPathsExactly for exact-string paths and the forbidden path shapes; TestArtifactCarriesRetirementAndStalenessApart for live-versus-stale; TestFreeStandingSupersessionStillRequiresAuthorOrRatifier for bare supersession authority; TestRetiredArtifactMarksDependentsAsDescribingASupersededWorld for the world-stale edge; TestMergeReceiptReachesOnlyWhatItsSuccessorCovers for the first-parent diff rule; and internal/docset's TestUnmaintainablePathNamesEveryShapeSuccessionCannotMaintain, which literally exercises the string \"AGENTS.md,SKILL.md\". Everything else removed survives verbatim in notes/retire-dot-artifacts.md, in SKILL.md, or in the merge.md succession table.\n\nONE RULE DID NOT FULLY SURVIVE AND I AM NAMING IT RATHER THAN LETTING IT PASS. Old lines 121-124 advised picking \"the granularity a reader would cite, a package directory or a document\" when no live artifact covers a change. gs merge now publishes a first artifact at the changed path automatically and SKILL.md says to reuse the exact string the area already uses, so the operative behaviour is covered — but the explicit \"package directory or a document\" hint is human judgement no test can check, and it is now in no file. That is a real, if small, loss. I would rather report it than claim a clean sweep.\n\nTHREE PASSAGES LEFT ALONE UNDER CONDITION 6, because any rewording risked shifting the rule: the describes_superseded_world propagation clause, which is precise about crossing a direct retired-artifact edge and then following artifact-to-artifact provenance only; the step 5 closure doctrine, where receipt-as-acceptance and no-implementation-ratification are the pair people invert; and the whole self-initiated-work exception.\n\nTHE MOVE IS BYTE-FOR-BYTE. notes/retire-dot-artifacts.md is new, 271 lines, of which 261 are old AGENTS.md lines 141-401 moved unchanged. I proved it mechanically rather than by eye: diffing the old range against the new file's lines 11-271 produces no output, and all five sh/jq blocks are present and identical. AGENTS.md keeps one pointer paragraph naming the migration, its preconditions and its gate.\n\nONE CORRECTION CARRIED ALONG: old line 60 read \"any opportunity to asimplify\". It now reads \"simplify\". No semantic content.\n\nWHAT I REJECTED FROM THE STARTING POINT, and it matters. Branch request/agents-md-simplification at 4c7c39bc does the same mechanical move, and reviving it would have been a silent semantics regression on the two rules this repository gets wrong most often. Its step 3 says to report ready-for-review against the promise; current main says the artifact IS the report and forbids the duplicate. Its step 5 says the requester ratifies the implementation report; current main says the sealed merge receipt is the pre-authorized acceptance and no implementation ratification follows. I took only its core decision, its file name and roughly four lines of pointer prose, and re-cut everything else from current main.\n\nGates at this exact head, run with -count=1 rather than bare make test so nothing came from cache: make vet exit 0; go test -count=1 ./... exit 0 across 28 packages with no FAIL and no (cached); make docs ok in 47.3s; make build exit 0; gofmt -l . empty; git status --porcelain empty. The docset gate could not have been at risk here — it walks docs/ only, and AGENTS.md carries no git:sha1 citations — but it is green regardless.\n\nEvery in-tree reference to AGENTS.md still reads true, checked individually: docs/reference/architecture.md:623 and :645 on the three review conclusions, notes/2026-08-20-composite-kinds.md at four places quoting steps 1 and 3, notes/2026-08-18-test-staleness-flare.md:207 on the `.` mutex warning — which is why the mutex reason is restored into step 5 rather than only the flares-nothing reason — SKILL.md:211, and internal/docset/docset.go:64, which only stats the file.\n\nThis artifact covers AGENTS.md. The companion first artifact at notes/retire-dot-artifacts.md stands at this same head and must be co-signed with it.","body":{"commit":"1ad16e7ee87442b560712cc18de99627b3b662c3","path":"AGENTS.md"}}